WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.584
Factory makes AI changes reviewable.

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.656
This small demo app has one deliberate bug.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.568
The Open list should hide completed tasks. On this known baseline, it still shows them.

4
00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:30.651
The Board shows the work. Decisions stay on the task and run pages.

5
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.808
The request states the expected result and the files the agent may change.

6
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:55.707
Each live call needs its own approval and money limit.

7
00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:11.525
The agent proposes a change. Factory records the attempt and its result.

8
00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:17.741
This attempt passed the configured checks and stayed within scope.

9
00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:26.014
Build, tests, acceptance checks, and browser evidence support review.

10
00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:33.550
The new regression tests failed on the original bug and passed on the fixed candidate.

11
00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:44.819
The reviewer compares the change with the request and records a decision.

12
00:01:52.867 --> 00:01:58.987
Here, Codex reviewed the result at the owner's request. This is not an independent human review.

13
00:02:06.867 --> 00:02:11.811
The owner approved this agent review. Human review minutes remain unknown.

14
00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:22.777
Approval can lead to a draft pull request with the verified files.

15
00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:35.377
The draft passed CI on the published commit. Merge remains a separate decision.

16
00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:44.409
This example shows the workflow. It does not establish general reliability or time savings.

17
00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:52.609
The triage agent read a document describing the known fix. This was not a blind evaluation.

18
00:02:55.801 --> 00:03:01.009
The demo fix remains in a draft pull request. It was not merged or deployed.
